#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:21
msgid ""
"Only Prices configured with matching Price Units can be used in a Price Set."
" \"Month\" is equivalent to 30 days by default. For AWS, month is 30.5 days."
" For Azure, month is 30.4 days."
msgstr ""
"Solo Precios configurado con matching Precio Units puede ser usado en a "
"Precio Establecido. \"Month\" es equivalent a 30 days de forma "
"predeterminada. Para AWS, month es 30.5 days. Para Azure, month es 30.4 "
"days."

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:34
msgid "Type"
msgstr "Tipo"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:24
msgid ""
"Price Set types determine which Prices are available to make up the set. "
"This selection will filter the values returned in the Prices field at the "
"bottom of the modal."
msgstr ""
"Precio Establecido tipos determine que Precios están disponibles a make up "
"el establecido. Este selection va a filter el valores returned en el Precios"
" campo en el bottom de el modal."

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:26
msgid ""
"It's helpful to make note of the Prices options below before creating Price "
"Sets."
msgstr ""
"It's helpful a make note de el Precios opciones below antes de creando "
"Precio Sets."

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:28
msgid ""
"**Everything:** 'Everything' price sets require one or more 'Everything' "
"price types and may include 'Platform' or 'Software' price types"
msgstr ""
"**Everything:** 'Everything' precio sets requerir uno o más 'Everything' "
"precio tipos y puede include 'Platform' o 'Software' precio tipos"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:29
msgid ""
"**Compute + Storage:** 'Compute + Storage' price sets require at least one "
"of each 'Memory',  CPU', and 'Disk Only' price types and may include "
"'Platform' or 'Software' price types"
msgstr ""
"**Compute + Storage:** 'Compute + Storage' precio sets requerir en least uno"
" de cada 'Memory', CPU', y 'Disk Solo' precio tipos y puede include "
"'Platform' o 'Software' precio tipos"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:30
msgid ""
"**Component:** 'Component' price sets require at least one of each 'Memory',"
" 'Cores', 'CPU', and 'Storage' price types and may include 'Platform' or "
"'Software' price types"
msgstr ""
"**Component:** 'Component' precio sets requerir en least uno de cada "
"'Memory', 'Cores', 'CPU', y 'Storage' precio tipos y puede include "
"'Platform' o 'Software' precio tipos"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:31
msgid ""
"**Load Balancer:** 'Load Balancer' price sets require at least one 'Load "
"Balancer' price type and may include 'Load Balancer Virtual Server' price "
"types. Load Balancer price sets are the only type which can be associated "
"with Load Balancer Price Plans"
msgstr ""
"**Load Balancer:** 'Load Balancer' precio sets requerir en least uno 'Load "
"Balancer' precio tipo y puede include 'Load Balancer Virtual Servidor' "
"precio tipos. Load Balancer precio sets son el solo tipo que puede ser "
"asociado con Load Balancer Precio Planes"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:32
msgid ""
"**Virtual Image:** 'Virtual Image' price sets require at least one 'Storage'"
" price type. Virtual Image price sets are the only type which can be "
"associated with Virtual Image Price plans"
msgstr ""
"**Virtual Image:** 'Virtual Image' precio sets requerir en least uno "
"'Storage' precio tipo. Virtual Image precio sets son el solo tipo que puede "
"ser asociado con Virtual Image Precio planes"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:33
msgid ""
"**Snapshot:** 'Snapshot' price sets require at least one 'Storage' price "
"type and may also include 'Datastore' price types. Snapshot price sets are "
"the only type which can be associated with Snapshot Price plans"
msgstr ""
"**Snapshot:** 'Snapshot' precio sets requerir en least uno 'Storage' precio "
"tipo y puede también include 'Datastore' precio tipos. Snapshot precio sets "
"son el solo tipo que puede ser asociado con Snapshot Precio planes"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:34
msgid ""
"**Software/Service:** 'Software/Service' Price Sets require at least one "
"'Software/Service' Price type"
msgstr ""
"**Software/Service:** 'Software/Service' Precio Sets requerir en least uno "
"'Software/Service' Precio tipo"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:37
#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:126
msgid "Apply Price Changes to Usage"
msgstr "Aplicar Precio Changes a Usage"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:37
#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:127
msgid ""
"If marked, when saving a Price Set (new Price Set or saving changes to an "
"existing one), usage records will be restarted for servers affected by the "
"pricing change."
msgstr ""
"Si marked, cuando saving a Precio Establecido (nuevo Precio Establecido o "
"saving changes a un existente uno), usage records será restarted para "
"servidores affected por el pricing change."

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:40
#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:46
msgid "Prices"
msgstr "Precios"

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:40
msgid ""
"Search for and select Prices to be added to the Price Set. One of each Price"
" Type required for the Price Set Type selected must be added for the Price "
"Set to save."
msgstr ""
"Search para y seleccionar Precios a be agregado a el Precio Establecido. Uno"
" de cada Precio Tipo requerido para el Precio Establecido Tipo seleccionado "
"debe ser agregado para el Precio Establecido a save."

#: ../../administration/plans_pricing/prices.rst:48
msgid ""
"Details on various price configurations are given here. When creating "
"prices, it's also necessary to understand how they will be applied. "
"Specifically, this relates to the **INCUR CHARGES** configuration. Charges "
"can be incurred \"While Running\", \"While Stopped\", or \"Always\". It "
"typically makes the most sense to have running and stopped prices for a "
"given type (Cores, for example) *OR* to have an \"Always\" price (but not "
"both). This is because the prices do not stack and the higher of a competing"
" \"Always\" or running/stopped price will take precedence. This can lead to "
"confusion over which price was applied and how a final cost total was "
"computed. You should decide in advance for a given price type for a price "
"set whether you wish to charge an \"Always\" rate or charge separately for "
"running/stopped states."
msgstr ""
"Detalles en various precio configurations son given here. Cuando creando "
"precios, ello's también necessary a understand how ellos será aplicado. "
"Specifically, este relates a el **INCUR CHARGES** configuración. Charges "
"puede ser incurred \"While Running\", \"While Stopped\", o \"Always\". It "
"typically makes el la mayoría de sense a tienen running y stopped precios "
"para a given tipo (Cores, por ejemplo) *OR* a tienen un \"Always\" precio "
"(pero no both). Este es because el precios hacer no stack y el higher de a "
"competing \"Always\" o running/stopped precio va a take precedence. Este "
"puede lead a confusion over que precio fue aplicado y how a final cost total"
" fue computed. You debería decide en advance para a given precio tipo para a"
" precio establecido whether usted wish a charge un \"Always\" rate o charge "
"separately para running/stopped states."

